# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
lib/
lib64/

# `lib/` above comes from the Python packaging boilerplate and, having no
# leading slash, git applies it at EVERY level -- so it also swallows
# application source directories named lib/. Re-include those here.
# This one is not cosmetic: without it the Vite build fails outright with
# "Could not resolve ./lib/shk.js", because the files are absent from the
# clone while `git status` reports a clean tree.
!enzymes/web/src/lib/
!enzymes/web/src/lib/**
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg

